IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `ssc-core`
IMPORT `ssc9-sch9-10`

-- Tests for ssc9-sch9-10.l4 (Schedules 9 and 10). Expected values are written by hand from the text, beside each assertion.

§ `Tests -- Schedules 9 and 10`

§§ `Schedule 9`

-- Argument order: detention; compulsory supervision order and residential establishment; in the care of a local authority in prescribed circumstances; regulations otherwise provide.
#ASSERT `sch 9 para 1 the person may be entitled to child benefit for the week` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `sch 9 para 1 the person may be entitled to child benefit for the week` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `sch 9 para 1 the person may be entitled to child benefit for the week` FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `sch 9 para 1 the person may be entitled to child benefit for the week` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- None of the three, or regulations otherwise provide: the paragraph does not bar (NOTHING, not an entitlement).
#ASSERT `sch 9 para 1 the person may be entitled to child benefit for the week` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `sch 9 para 1 the person may be entitled to child benefit for the week` TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `sch 9 para 3 the person may be entitled to child benefit for the child or qualifying young person` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `sch 9 para 3 the person may be entitled to child benefit for the child or qualifying young person` TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `sch 9 para 3 the person may be entitled to child benefit for the child or qualifying young person` FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

§§ `Schedule 10 paragraph 1 -- prior award`

-- The prior award holder is the one entitled when the week claimed is up to the third week after the claim; the claimant is not.
#ASSERT `sch 10 para 1 the person is the one entitled` `sch 10 para 1 the person has already been awarded child benefit when the other claims` 0 EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `sch 10 para 1 the person is the one entitled` `sch 10 para 1 the person has already been awarded child benefit when the other claims` 3 EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `sch 10 para 1 the person is the one entitled` `sch 10 para 1 the person is the one claiming` 3 EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `sch 10 para 1 the person is the one entitled` `sch 10 para 1 the person is the one claiming` 0 EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- The fourth week after the claim: no priority.
#ASSERT `sch 10 para 1 the person is the one entitled` `sch 10 para 1 the person has already been awarded child benefit when the other claims` 4 EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `sch 10 para 1 the person is the one entitled` `sch 10 para 1 the person is the one claiming` 4 EQUALS NOTHING

§§ `Schedule 10 paragraphs 2 and 3`

-- Argument order: paragraph 1 decides; my (a); my (b); other's (a); other's (b).
#ASSERT `sch 10 para 2 the person is the one entitled` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `sch 10 para 2 the person is the one entitled` FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `sch 10 para 2 the person is the one entitled` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `sch 10 para 2 the person is the one entitled` FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `sch 10 para 2 the person is the one entitled` FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
-- Argument order: paragraph 1 or 2 decides; man and woman married or civil partners residing together; the person's sex.
#ASSERT `sch 10 para 3 the person is the one entitled` FALSE TRUE Woman EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `sch 10 para 3 the person is the one entitled` FALSE TRUE Man EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `sch 10 para 3 the person is the one entitled` TRUE TRUE Woman EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `sch 10 para 3 the person is the one entitled` FALSE FALSE Woman EQUALS NOTHING

§§ `Schedule 10 paragraph 4 -- parents`

-- 4(1): argument order: earlier paragraphs decide; I am a parent; the other is a parent.
#ASSERT `sch 10 para 4(1) the person is the one entitled` FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `sch 10 para 4(1) the person is the one entitled` FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `sch 10 para 4(1) the person is the one entitled` FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `sch 10 para 4(1) the person is the one entitled` FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `sch 10 para 4(1) the person is the one entitled` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- 4(2): argument order: earlier decide; both parents residing together; I am the mother; the other is the mother.
#ASSERT `sch 10 para 4(2) the person is the one entitled` FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `sch 10 para 4(2) the person is the one entitled` FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `sch 10 para 4(2) the person is the one entitled` FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `sch 10 para 4(2) the person is the one entitled` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `sch 10 para 4(2) the person is the one entitled` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `sch 10 para 4(2) the person is the one entitled` FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

§§ `Schedule 10 paragraphs 5 and 6`

-- 5: argument order: earlier paragraphs decide; the election; made in the prescribed manner; the Secretary of State's determination.
#ASSERT `sch 10 para 5 the person is the one entitled` FALSE `sch 10 para 5 the persons have jointly elected the person` TRUE NOTHING EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `sch 10 para 5 the person is the one entitled` FALSE `sch 10 para 5 the persons have jointly elected the other person` TRUE NOTHING EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- An election not made in the prescribed manner: 6(1) says elections shall be so made and does not say what follows, so NOTHING, whatever the Secretary of State's determination.
#ASSERT `sch 10 para 5 the person is the one entitled` FALSE `sch 10 para 5 the persons have jointly elected the person` FALSE NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `sch 10 para 5 the person is the one entitled` FALSE `sch 10 para 5 the persons have jointly elected the person` FALSE (JUST FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING
-- No election: the determination, if made.
#ASSERT `sch 10 para 5 the person is the one entitled` FALSE `sch 10 para 5 the persons have not jointly elected` TRUE (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `sch 10 para 5 the person is the one entitled` FALSE `sch 10 para 5 the persons have not jointly elected` TRUE NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `sch 10 para 5 the person is the one entitled` TRUE `sch 10 para 5 the persons have jointly elected the person` TRUE (JUST TRUE) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `sch 10 para 6(1) the election is an election under this Schedule` TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `sch 10 para 6(1) the election is an election under this Schedule` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
